  {
    "name": "pluralize",
    "line": 1,
    "pseudocode": "pluralize(word: bytes) -> bytes\n\nUNCOUNTABLE = [ \"equipment\", \"information\", \"rice\", \"money\",\n                \"species\", \"series\", \"fish\", \"sheep\",\n                \"jeans\", \"police\" ]      // exactly these 10, in this order\n\n1. If word (the WHOLE byte string, no trimming, no lowercasing, no word-boundary\n   search) is byte-for-byte EQUAL to any entry of UNCOUNTABLE:\n       return word unchanged (a copy).\n2. Otherwise:\n       return word with the single byte 0x73 ('s') appended.\n\nThat is the entire rule. There is NO other transformation:\n  - no y->ies      (city -> \"citys\",  baby -> \"babys\",  fly -> \"flys\")\n  - no x/ch/ss/sh->es (box -> \"boxs\", church -> \"churchs\", class -> \"classs\", dish -> \"dishs\")\n  - no o->oes      (tomato -> \"tomatos\", potato -> \"potatos\", hero -> \"heros\")\n  - no f/fe->ves   (leaf -> \"leafs\",  knife -> \"knifes\", wolf -> \"wolfs\")\n  - no is->es      (axis -> \"axiss\",  analysis -> \"analysiss\", crisis -> \"crisiss\")\n  - no us->i       (octopus -> \"octopuss\", virus -> \"viruss\", cactus -> \"cactuss\")\n  - no um/on->a    (datum -> \"datums\", medium -> \"mediums\", criterion -> \"criterions\")\n  - no ix/ex->ices (matrix -> \"matrixs\", vertex -> \"vertexs\", index -> \"indexs\")\n  - no ouse->ice   (mouse -> \"mouses\", louse -> \"louses\")\n  - no bus->buses  (bus -> \"buss\"),  no quiz->quizzes (quiz -> \"quizs\")\n  - no ox->oxen    (ox -> \"oxs\")\n  - no alias/status->es (alias -> \"aliass\", status -> \"statuss\")\n  - no (n)ews rule (news -> \"newss\")\n  - no irregular map (man -> \"mans\", child -> \"childs\", person -> \"persons\",\n     tooth -> \"tooths\", foot -> \"foots\", goose -> \"gooses\", people -> \"peoples\")\n  - no \"already plural -> unchanged\" check (boxes -> \"boxess\", fishes -> \"fishess\",\n     mice -> \"mices\", children -> \"childrens\", data -> \"datas\")\n\nMATCHING DETAILS (all probed):\n  - CASE-SENSITIVE: \"Sheep\" -> \"Sheeps\", \"SHEEP\" -> \"SHEEPs\", \"sHeep\" -> \"sHeeps\",\n    \"ShEeP\" -> \"ShEePs\", \"Fish\" -> \"Fishs\", \"FISH\" -> \"FISHs\", \"Money\" -> \"Moneys\",\n    \"POLICE\" -> \"POLICEs\", \"JEANS\" -> \"JEANSs\", \"Equipment\" -> \"Equipments\".\n    Only the all-lowercase spelling is uncountable.\n  - WHOLE-STRING equality, NOT a suffix/regex/word-boundary match:\n    \"goldfish\" -> \"goldfishs\", \"bluefish\" -> \"bluefishs\", \"xfish\" -> \"xfishs\",\n    \"fishx\" -> \"fishxs\", \"gold fish\" -> \"gold fishs\", \"a fish\" -> \"a fishs\",\n    \"gold-fish\" -> \"gold-fishs\", \"x_fish\" -> \"x_fishs\", \"the police\" -> \"the polices\",\n    \"blacksheep\" -> \"blacksheeps\", \"xseries\" -> \"xseriess\".\n  - NO whitespace trimming before compare: \"fish \" -> \"fish s\", \" fish\" -> \" fishs\".\n  - Purely byte-based, locale/encoding agnostic: bytes >= 0x80 pass through and get\n    an 's' appended (\"caf\\xc3\\xa9\" -> \"caf\\xc3\\xa9s\", \"\\xff\" -> \"\\xffs\",\n    \"\\x80\\x81\" -> \"\\x80\\x81s\", \"\\xe4\\xb8\\xad\\xe6\\x96\\x87\" -> that + \"s\").\n  - Control bytes pass through: \"a\\tb\" -> \"a\\tbs\".\n  - Length independent: 100000 'a' bytes -> 100001 bytes ending in 's'.\n  - Empty input never reaches a normal return in this program: the harness aborts in\n    line 18 (demodulize) with std::out_of_range before any stdout flush, so nothing\n    is printed. As a function, pluralize(\"\") would return \"s\" by the rule above\n    (unverifiable in isolation from this binary).",
    "rust_sketch": "const UNCOUNTABLE: [&str; 10] = [\n    \"equipment\", \"information\", \"rice\", \"money\", \"species\",\n    \"series\", \"fish\", \"sheep\", \"jeans\", \"police\",\n];\n\n/// Byte-exact reimplementation of line 1 of test20_executable.\npub fn pluralize(word: &[u8]) -> Vec<u8> {\n    // Whole-string, case-sensitive, byte-for-byte comparison.\n    for u in UNCOUNTABLE.iter() {\n        if word == u.as_bytes() {\n            return word.to_vec();\n        }\n    }\n    let mut out = Vec::with_capacity(word.len() + 1);\n    out.extend_from_slice(word);\n    out.push(b's');\n    out\n}\n\n// String convenience wrapper (input may be non-UTF8 in general; prefer &[u8]).\npub fn pluralize_str(word: &str) -> String {\n    if UNCOUNTABLE.contains(&word) {\n        word.to_string()\n    } else {\n        let mut s = String::with_capacity(word.len() + 1);\n        s.push_str(word);\n        s.push('s');\n        s\n    }\n}",
